-- title:
--   Locally constant functions on Spec T refine into idempotents
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring, let $Y$ be any type, and let $f : \operatorname{Spec} T \to Y$ be a function on the prime spectrum which is locally constant, i.e. satisfies `IsLocallyConstant f`. The assertion is that there exist a natural number $n$ and a family $e : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to T$ with the following three properties. First, $e$ is a complete orthogonal family of idempotents in the sense of Mathlib's `CompleteOrthogonalIdempotents`: each $e_k$ is idempotent, $e_k e_l = 0$ whenever $k \neq l$, and $\sum_{k} e_k = 1$. Second, the ideal generated by the set $\{e_k\}$ is the unit ideal, $\mathrm{span}(\operatorname{range} e) = \top$ (a consequence of $\sum_k e_k = 1$, recorded separately). Third, $f$ is constant on each of the basic open sets cut out by the family: for every $k$ there is an element $c \in Y$ such that $f(x) = c$ for all $x \in \operatorname{Spec} T$ lying in $D(e_k) =$ `PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen (e k)`. No finiteness, separatedness or other hypothesis on $Y$ is imposed; degenerate cases such as $T = 0$ (with $n = 0$) and $e_k = 0$ (with $D(e_k) = \emptyset$) are permitted.
--
--   This is the standard translation, for the spectrum of a commutative ring, between clopen decompositions of $\operatorname{Spec} T$ and complete orthogonal families of idempotents of $T$, in the form that a locally constant function on $\operatorname{Spec} T$ is refined by such a family. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_strata_point_locally_corr_of_span_eq_top`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_strata_point_locally_corr_of_span_eq_top) invokes it to split a base ring according to a locally constant invariant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PrimeSpectrum_exists_completeOrthogonalIdempotents_forall_apply_eq_of_isLocallyConstant.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem PrimeSpectrum.exists_completeOrthogonalIdempotents_forall_apply_eq_of_isLocallyConstant
    {T : Type*} [CommRing T] {Y : Type*} (f : PrimeSpectrum T → Y) (hf : IsLocallyConstant f) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (e : Fin n → T),
      CompleteOrthogonalIdempotents e ∧ Ideal.span (Set.range e) = ⊤ ∧
      ∀ k : Fin n, ∃ c : Y, ∀ x : PrimeSpectrum T, x ∈ PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen (e k) → f x = c := by sorry
